### ❌ `N8N-BE-204` — Zero Dead-End Conditional Branches [CRITICAL]
**Issue**: Conditional nodes (`n8n-nodes-base.if`, `n8n-nodes-base.switch`, `n8n-nodes-base.filter`) must wire every defined output branch (e.g. both `true` (index 0) and `false` (index 1)) to downstream processing or recovery nodes.
**Fix**: `connections[ifNode.name].main` must have non-empty connection arrays for both index 0 and index 1.
```diff
- An IF node where index 0 (`true`) routes to Slack, but index 1 (`false`) is left unhandled with `[]`.
+ [Compliant fix]
```

**Corrected code:**
```
{
  "name": "Dead End IF Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Check Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        100,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Handle True",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        300,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Handle False",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        300,
        300
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Check Lead": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Handle True",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Handle False",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
