### ❌ `N8N-BE-205` — Zero Dangling Final Catch / Error Handlers [CRITICAL]
**Issue**: Nodes configured with `"onError": "continueErrorOutput"` must connect their second output index (error branch) to an explicit alert, logging, or fallback node.
**Fix**: When `node.onError === 'continueErrorOutput'`, `connections[node.name].main[1]` must contain at least 1 destination node.
```diff
- A node with `onError = continueErrorOutput` but no wires connected to the error output connector.
+ [Compliant fix]
```

**Corrected code:**
```
{
  "name": "Dangling Catch Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "API Call",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        100,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Error Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        300,
        300
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "API Call": {
      "main": [
        [],
        [
          {
